    "notes": "The Beijing Railway Station model includes the two clock towers and three recessed entrance bays, both open courtyards, eight rows of platform roofs, and the elevated passenger connector with supported stairs. Forecourt and platform elevations are visual estimates from the mapped plan and standard terrain. The platform roofs use locally fitted support heights and retain the eight modeled rows and existing rail gaps. The model depicts the permanent passenger exterior. Fine thresholds, hidden rooms and temporary works are approximate or outside the model scope."
  },
